  "baseline": "each operator raises NotImplementedError on an MPS tensor without the overlay",
  "timing": "three numbers per operator, because the box is shared and one number cannot separate code from load. cpu_ms is the best of 30 CPU runs; mps_ms is the best of 30 MPS runs with torch.mps.synchronize() after each, so it is dominated by the device round trip (about 0.12 ms here) rather than by the kernel, and speedup = cpu_ms / mps_ms carries that bias against MPS. before_ms/after_ms come from one interleaved batch: the aten composite and the fused operator run back to back, order alternating, eight launches between synchronizations, minimum per variant, next to a copy_ of the same bytes as the floor; ratio = before_ms / after_ms is the code comparison and ratio_median is the median of the per-pair ratios. speedup_amortized = cpu_ms / after_ms compares the CPU cost, which has no queue to drain, with the amortized MPS cost",
  "not_measured": {
    "_fused_sdp_choice": "returns an SDPBackend enum value; no tensor work to time"
  },
